1. [MAJOR] tests/checkpoint_ancestry_test.rs:203 — resolve_main prefers refs/heads/main whenever it exists with no check that it agrees with refs/remotes/origin/main — the repair at ensure_full_history fetches only into refs/remotes/origin/*, so a local main that fell behind stays behind and is then audited — new checkpoints on origin/main after the clone are missed and a stale history reads as clean, the exact false pass this audit exists to prevent; the doc claim that both refs name the same commits is untrue when diverged — audit refs/remotes/origin/main after the fetch, or resolve both refs and refuse unless tips match, plus a divergent-tips test
